// "Coteau Citrouille": a hillside of pumpkins at dusk (issue #111, the 11th circuit), after the
// guide « Conception des circuits » (docs/GAME_DESIGN.md § 16). Original layout, about 1680 m a
// lap, turning right: the start straight in the pumpkin field, 10 m above the valley; two
// hairpins (right, left) up the hillside; issue #219: the climb on north (steep, in
// anti-gravity), into **the loop** (to the left, 270°), which climbs all the way round and comes
// out of it **on a bridge over the road that came up to it**, 14 m under it (the road passes
// over itself, GD § 16, rule 3); east along the top, 44 m up, down a drop; the lacets of the top
// (a hairpin to the right, a hairpin to the left) up to the crest, 48 m up (20 m before #219);
// the risky jump's corner (a tight corner to the right, its inside a drop, that a ramp crosses);
// down the hillside: a tight corner, the serpentine (a hairpin to the left, a hairpin to the
// right; its two legs steep, in anti-gravity) down to the field, a bump; the bulge round a giant
// crooked pine, whose hidden road runs straight behind a stack of crates; the last corner, that
// the grass bridge crosses behind a curtain of tall grass; a bump on the way back to the line.
// Six hairpins of 180° (a Normal bot drifts them), the loop of 270° (a tight corner of 90° to the
// right before #219: the same way out), the bulge's S (left 75°, right 150°, left 75°), three
// tight corners of 90°: no long soft curve, one long straight. The pieces of the shortcuts (the
// jump's corner and its landing; the bulge, the last corner and their paths) are the Corniche
// Cannelle's (issues #107, #156: their gains and their hiding were tuned), with other covers; the
// rest is new.
//
// Drawn as a plan of straights and arcs, its points every 8 m along it (the parameters below
// follow them).
//
// Format: see src/track/data.rs. Point 0 is the start line; karts drive toward point 1 (north,
// -Z), then turn right. The grid sits on the straight behind point 0.
(
    name: "Coteau Citrouille",
    // Dressing (issue #11): the pumpkin hillside at dusk (`assets/data/biomes.ron`), the same every
    // time (seed), and pieces placed by hand: checkered flags at the start line, a giant crooked
    // pine that hides the hidden road, a giant carved pumpkin by the jump's corner.
    biome: "Citrouilles",
    // Issue #104: its music (`assets/data/music.ron`).
    music: "neon-sign-circuit",
    decor_seed: 111,
    // Issue #211: the pumpkin hillside's terrain (`assets/data/biomes.ron`), and it hugs the road:
    // the road, 10 to 48 m above the valley all the way round (issue #219: 20 m at most before), is
    // carried by the hillside up to its walls, which falls away from them (`embank`, rise over run:
    // about 31°), instead of the skirts down to the flat valley. The voids stay (the jump's corner:
    // 6 m under the road at least). Issue #219: its hills 50 m high (32 m before), above the crest.
    terrain: (height: 50.0, scale: 140.0, floor: 0.25, rock: (0.46, 0.37, 0.28), embank: 0.6),
    props: [
        (model: "racing-kit/flagCheckers", at: 0.0, side: Both, height: 4.0, radius: 0.9, gap: 1.8),
        (model: "graveyard-kit/pine-crooked", at: 178.216, side: Right, height: 24.0, radius: 3.8, gap: 8.0),
        (model: "graveyard-kit/pumpkin-tall-carved", at: 111.204, side: Left, height: 14.0, radius: 6.0, gap: 2.0),
    ],
    checkpoint_spacing: 25.0,
    points: [
